{
  "mn45:0.1": "Middle Discourses 45 ",
  "mn45:0.2": "The Shorter Discourse on Taking Up Practices ",
  "mn45:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn45:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn45:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn45:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn45:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn45:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn45:2.1": "“Mendicants, there are these four ways of taking up practices. ",
  "mn45:2.2": "What four? ",
  "mn45:2.3": "There is a way of taking up practices that is pleasant now but results in future pain. ",
  "mn45:2.4": "There is a way of taking up practices that is painful now and results in future pain. ",
  "mn45:2.5": "There is a way of taking up practices that is painful now but results in future pleasure. ",
  "mn45:2.6": "There is a way of taking up practices that is pleasant now and results in future pleasure. ",
  "mn45:3.1": "And what is the way of taking up practices that is pleasant now but results in future pain? ",
  "mn45:3.2": "There are some ascetics and brahmins who have this doctrine and view: ",
  "mn45:3.3": "‘There’s nothing wrong with sensual pleasures.’ ",
  "mn45:3.4": "They throw themselves into sensual pleasures, ",
  "mn45:3.5": "cavorting with female wanderers with jeweled bands in their hair. ",
  "mn45:3.6": "They say, ",
  "mn45:3.7": "‘What future danger do those ascetics and brahmins see in sensual pleasures that the